# Pre-commit (repave)

Run from **repo root** before every commit.

## Standard loop (runtime code)

When the diff touches **runtime code** (`engine/`, `operator/`, `scripts/**/*.py`,
`deploy/k8s/chart/templates/**`, portal JS, workflows, etc.):

```bash
make format && make quality && make test
```

When the diff can change **blueprint render output** (`blueprints/**`,
`engine/**/backstage_catalog.py`, `engine/**/render.py`, catalog emit paths), also:

```bash
make blueprint-conformance-check
```

If the check reports drift, refresh committed manifests in the same PR:

```bash
make blueprint-conformance-update && make blueprint-conformance-check
```

**Docs-only commits** (for example `docs/**`, `README.md`, roadmap housecleaning) skip
the loop above unless the same commit also changes runtime paths.

Before opening a PR that touches **any Python** (`**/*.py`), also run **`make security`**
when the diff includes **`engine/`**; for **scripts-only** Python, run Ruff and Bandit
on the changed paths (see **repave-python** skill).

- **`make format`** — `ruff format` on `engine/src` and `engine/tests` (run Ruff on other `.py` paths manually)
- **`make quality`** — `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, **`mypy src`**
- **`make test`** — full pytest + coverage threshold (75%)

While editing Python, **`make test-fast`** skips `@pytest.mark.slow` and coverage.

## When to add checks

| Change | Also run |
|--------|----------|
| Any **`*.py`** | Follow `.cursor/rules/python-standards.mdc` and `python-security.mdc` |
| `engine/` Python | **`make security`** (Bandit + pip-audit — same as CI) |
| `scripts/` or other `.py` | `cd engine && uv run ruff check/format` on changed paths; Bandit if security-relevant |
| `operator/` | **`make operator-lint`** and **`make operator-test`**; follow `golang-standards.mdc` / `golang-security.mdc` |
| `engine/pyproject.toml` deps | `make lock` and commit `engine/uv.lock` |
| Any **`*.js` / `*.mjs` / `*.cjs`** | **`make js-lint`**; follow `javascript-standards.mdc` / `javascript-security.mdc` |
| **`deploy/k8s/chart/**`** (templates, values, validate script) | **`make chart-validate`** |
| **`blueprints/**`** or catalog emit (`backstage_catalog.py`, `render.py`, `pipeline.py` catalog paths) | **`make blueprint-conformance-check`**; on drift **`make blueprint-conformance-update`** and commit `conformance.manifest*.json` |
| **Roadmap + docs housecleaning** (see below) | Checklist only — **not** `chart-validate` unless chart paths are in the diff |

## Roadmap and docs housecleaning

When a PR **ships**, **supersedes**, or **closes** a roadmap theme, include doc
housecleaning in the **same PR** (or an immediate follow-up). This is separate from
Helm/chart validation — run `make chart-validate` only when chart files change.

### `docs/roadmap.md` (feature PRs)

- Do **not** edit **Current release** — Release owns it (`sync_doc_versions.py`).
- Update **In progress** and **Shipped on `main`** at the top.
- Update the theme table and path-to-v2 tree when status changes.
- Set section `**Status:**` for every theme touched; remove stale branch names,
  `Not started`, and “blocked behind” wording for shipped work.
- Mark superseded entries (for example old k8s deploy path) as **Superseded** with
  a link to the shipped replacement.

### Related docs (housecleaning)

- Cross-link new behavior from the doc that operators read (`docs/durability.md`,
  `docs/verify.md`, `docs/operations/**`, chart README, `deploy/k8s/README.md`).
- Align “still open” / follow-up bullets with the roadmap header — no contradictory
  shipped vs open claims across files.

### Pre-commit for docs-only work

```bash
# Optional: only if you edited version pointer lines Release normally owns
make sync-doc-versions --check
```

No `make format`, `make quality`, `make test`, or `make chart-validate` for a
docs-only roadmap/housecleaning commit.

## Commits and PRs

- Conventional commits; PR titles validated by CI (`semantic-pull-request` —
  subject must not start with uppercase) — see `.cursor/rules/pull-requests.mdc`.
- Ship **tests in the same PR** as new engine behavior unless the change is docs-only.

Details: `CONTRIBUTING.md`; Python: `.cursor/rules/python-standards.mdc`, security: `.cursor/rules/python-security.mdc`; JavaScript: `.cursor/rules/javascript-standards.mdc`, security: `.cursor/rules/javascript-security.mdc`; Go: `.cursor/rules/golang-standards.mdc`, security: `.cursor/rules/golang-security.mdc`.
